  "id": "coding",
  "term": "coding",
  "definition": "Coding is a subtest of the Wechsler Intelligence Scale for Children in which a child uses a key to match numbers with symbols and writes the correct symbol in boxes on the page. It is used to assess visual processing speed, short-term visual memory, efficient shifting of eye focus, and fine motor skill, without relying on expressive language.",
